[laptop] $ moolah init    # answers: n | EUR |  | $FOLDER | new
Created the encryption key $TMP/config/age-key.txt. Keep a copy somewhere safe; copy it to your other computers.
This book syncs through $FOLDER.
Book "main" is ready in $TMP/data/books/main.db (base currency EUR).
Next: add your accounts, for example:
  moolah account add assets:bank:mybank --currency EUR --opening 1000
  moolah category list
Do you already use moolah on another computer? [y/N]: Base currency (ISO code, for example USD, EUR, GBP): Language and number format (for example en_US, de_DE, he_IL) [en_US]: Sync folder for your other computers (Enter to skip; add one later with: moolah sync init <folder>): Encryption key for backups and sync: 'new' (create one), 'ssh' (~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub), a public key, or 'none' (a passphrase each time) [new]: 
[desktop] $ moolah init    # answers: y | $EMPTY
Do you already use moolah on another computer? [y/N]: Its sync folder (the folder your sync tool shares, for example ~/Dropbox/moolah): error: $EMPTY has no moolah data yet. Wait until your sync tool has copied it, then run moolah init again
[exit 1]

[desktop] $ moolah init    # answers: y | $FOLDER
